```c
/* area.c */
#include <stdio.h>
#define PI 3.14159
int main(void) {
    double r = 2.0;
    printf("%.2f\n", PI * r * r);
    return 0;
}
```

```bash
gcc -E area.c -o area.i     # 1. preprocessed: stdio.h pasted in, PI replaced.
gcc -S area.i -o area.s     # 2. compiled to assembly.
gcc -c area.s -o area.o     # 3. assembled: object file, printf still unresolved.
gcc area.o -o area          # 4. linked with the C library: printf resolved.
./area                      # 12.57
```

| Error looks like | Phase |
|---|---|
| `fatal error: stdio.hh: No such file`. | preprocess. |
| `expected ';' before 'return'`. | compile. |
| `undefined reference to 'area'`. | link. |

```reveal
{"prompt": "Why can each .c file compile but the program still fail?", "answer": "Compilation checks one translation unit at a time and only needs declarations. The linker is the first step that needs every definition, from all files and libraries, together."}
```

